  "analysis": "Cholestasis is the pathology that results from the arrest of bile flow, leading to bile accumulation in the liver and a lack of bile in the duodenum. This condition is characterized by impaired bile flow obstructing the passage of bile to the duodenum. Cholelithiasis refers to the presence of gallstones in the gallbladder or bile ducts, which can cause blockages but is not directly related to the arrest of bile flow. Cholangitis is inflammation of the bile ducts, often due to infection, and cholecystitis is inflammation of the gallbladder. While these conditions can impact bile flow, they do not specifically involve the arrest of bile flow as seen in cholestasis.",
